</table>

<h3>Authentication Ports</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Protocol</th><th>Port</th><th>Used by</th></tr>
<tr><td>SASL/SCRAM (TLS)</td><td>9096</td><td>Application clients on EC2 (credentials from Secrets Manager)</td></tr>
<tr><td>SASL/IAM (TLS)</td><td>9098</td><td>MSK Connect workers (AWS Signature v4 via IAM role)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Plaintext</td><td>9092</td><td>MSK Connect internal use (intra-VPC only)</td></tr>
<tr><td>TLS</td><td>9094</td><td>MSK Connect internal use (intra-VPC only)</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>4.2 Debezium Source Connector</h2>
<table>
<tr><th style="width:35%;">Setting</th><th>Value</th></tr>
<tr><td>Connector name</td><td>caltech-poc-debezium-postgres-source-connector</td></tr>
<tr><td>Connector class</td><td>io.debezium.connector.postgresql.PostgresConnector</td></tr>
<tr><td>PostgreSQL output plugin</td><td>pgoutput</td></tr>
<tr><td>Publication mode</td><td>all_tables (auto-create)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Topic prefix</td><td>caltech_poc_10</td></tr>
<tr><td>Topic naming pattern</td><td>caltech_poc_10.&lt;schema&gt;.&lt;table&gt;</td></tr>
<tr><td>Single Message Transform (SMT)</td><td>unwrap (io.debezium.transforms.ExtractNewRecordState)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Schemas.enable</td><td>false (schema-less JSON output)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Authentication to MSK</td><td>SASL/IAM (port 9098) via MSK Connect execution role</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>4.3 JDBC Sink Connectors (x5)</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Connector</th><th>Source topic</th><th>Sink table</th></tr>
<tr><td>postgres-sink-connector-student-enrollment</td><td>caltech_poc_10.public.student_enrollment</td><td>student_enrollment</td></tr>
<tr><td>postgres-sink-connector-student-attendance</td><td>caltech_poc_10.public.student_attendance</td><td>student_attendance</td></tr>
<tr><td>postgres-sink-connector-student-lms</td><td>caltech_poc_10.public.student_lms</td><td>student_lms</td></tr>
<tr><td>postgres-sink-connector-section-enrollments</td><td>caltech_poc_10.public.section_enrollments</td><td>section_enrollments</td></tr>
<tr><td>postgres-sink-connector-student-term-log</td><td>caltech_poc_10.public.student_term_log</td><td>student_term_log</td></tr>
</table>

<h4>Sink connector common settings</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Connector class:</strong> io.confluent.connect.jdbc.JdbcSinkConnector</li>
  <li><strong>Dialect:</strong> PostgreSqlDatabaseDialect</li>
  <li><strong>insert.mode:</strong> upsert (idempotent re-application of events)</li>
  <li><strong>pk.mode:</strong> record_key (uses Kafka message key as primary key)</li>
  <li><strong>auto.create / auto.evolve:</strong> true (schema-on-write to the sink)</li>
  <li><strong>delete.enabled:</strong> true (tombstone messages delete rows)</li>
  <li><strong>schemas.enable:</strong> false (matches source connector's schema-less output)</li>
  <li><strong>batch.size:</strong> 5000</li>
</ul>

</div>

<!-- ========================================================================
     5. SECURITY
     ======================================================================== -->
<div class="WordSection2">

<h1>5. Security Model</h1>

<h2>5.1 Encryption</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Service</th><th>At Rest</th><th>In Transit</th><th>KMS Alias</th></tr>
<tr><td>EC2 EBS volumes (x3)</td><td>KMS CMK</td><td>n/a</td><td>alias/caltech-poc-ebs</td></tr>
<tr><td>Aurora Source / Sink / Limitless</td><td>KMS CMK</td><td>TLS (rds.force_ssl=1)</td><td>alias/caltech-poc-aurora</td></tr>
<tr><td>MSK Provisioned</td><td>KMS CMK</td><td>TLS (broker&harr;client, in-cluster)</td><td>alias/caltech-poc-secrets</td></tr>
<tr><td>ElastiCache Redis</td><td>KMS CMK</td><td>TLS (always on)</td><td>alias/caltech-poc-redis</td></tr>
<tr><td>S3 buckets (x3)</td><td>KMS CMK</td><td>TLS</td><td>alias/caltech-poc-s3</td></tr>
<tr><td>Secrets Manager</td><td>KMS CMK</td><td>TLS</td><td>alias/caltech-poc-secrets</td></tr>
</table>
<p style="font-size:10pt;color:#595959;">All KMS keys have automatic yearly rotation enabled.</p>

<h2>5.2 Authentication &amp; Authorization</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Connection</th><th>Method</th></tr>
<tr><td>Engineer &rarr; EC2</td><td>AWS Systems Manager Session Manager (no SSH keys, no public IP, no bastion)</td></tr>
<tr><td>EC2 &rarr; MSK</td><td>SASL/SCRAM (port 9096), credentials from AWS Secrets Manager</td></tr>
<tr><td>MSK Connect &rarr; MSK</td><td>SASL/IAM (port 9098) using MSK Connect execution role</td></tr>
<tr><td>EC2 &rarr; Aurora (any cluster)</td><td>PostgreSQL password from AWS Secrets Manager</td></tr>
<tr><td>MSK Connect &rarr; Aurora Source</td><td>PostgreSQL password from Secrets Manager (Debezium configuration)</td></tr>
<tr><td>MSK Connect &rarr; Aurora Sink</td><td>PostgreSQL password from Secrets Manager (JDBC connection URL)</td></tr>
<tr><td>EC2 &rarr; ElastiCache Redis</td><td>VPC security group only (no auth token &mdash; TLS protects the link)</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>5.3 Security Group Matrix</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>From &darr; / To &rarr;</th><th>EC2</th><th>MSK</th><th>MSK Connect</th><th>Aurora Src</th><th>Aurora Sink</th><th>Redis</th></tr>
<tr><td><strong>EC2</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td>9098, 9096</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>5432</td><td>5432</td><td>6379</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>MSK Connect</strong></td><td>&mdash;</td><td>9098, 9096, 9092, 9094</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>5432</td><td>5432</td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>VM CIDR (10.145.0.0/24)</strong></td><td>22, 8080</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>&mdash;</td><td>5432</td><td>5432</td><td>6379</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>5.4 Network Isolation</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>No public IPs on EC2.</strong> All access via AWS Systems Manager Session Manager (over private VPC endpoints).</li>
  <li><strong>Aurora and ElastiCache live in private subnets</strong> with no Internet route.</li>
  <li><strong>Security groups follow least-privilege.</strong> Inbound rules are restricted to specific source SGs (e.g., Aurora Source SG accepts 5432 only from EC2 SG, MSK Connect SG, and the VM CIDR).</li>
  <li><strong>On-prem VM access</strong> is allowed only from the CIDR <code>10.145.0.0/24</code> on PostgreSQL (5432), Redis (6379), and EC2 SSH/app (22, 8080).</li>
  <li><strong>VPC Flow Logs</strong> can be enabled at the VPC level for audit and incident response (not managed by this stack).</li>
</ul>

<h2>5.5 Credential Handling</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>No plain-text passwords in code or in terraform.tfvars.</strong> Aurora master passwords are auto-generated by Terraform's <code>random_password</code> and stored exclusively in AWS Secrets Manager.</li>
  <li><strong>MSK SCRAM secret</strong> is auto-generated and associated with the cluster via <code>aws_msk_scram_secret_association</code>.</li>
  <li><strong>IAM least-privilege.</strong> The MSK Connect execution role has scoped permissions to read SCRAM secret, write CloudWatch logs, connect to MSK (specific cluster ARN), and read the S3 plugin bucket &mdash; and nothing else.</li>
  <li><strong>Final tightening.</strong> After all services are deployed, the EC2 and MSK Connect IAM policies are tightened from <code>"*"</code> to the exact MSK cluster ARN.</li>
</ul>

</div>

<!-- ========================================================================
     6. DEPLOYMENT SUMMARY
     ======================================================================== -->
<div class="WordSection2">

<h1>6. Deployment Summary</h1>

<p>The stack is deployed in six sequential phases that follow the data flow from left to right. Each phase produces an output that the next phase consumes.</p>

<table>
<tr><th>Phase</th><th>Module</th><th>Estimated Time</th><th>What it produces</th></tr>
<tr><td rowspan="6" style="vertical-align:middle;"><strong>1. Foundation</strong></td><td>kms</td><td>1 min</td><td>5 KMS keys</td></tr>
<tr><td>security_groups</td><td>1 min</td><td>7 security groups</td></tr>
<tr><td>vpc_endpoints</td><td>2 min</td><td>3 SSM interface endpoints + S3 Gateway</td></tr>
<tr><td>s3</td><td>1 min</td><td>3 S3 buckets (plugins, data-lake, logs)</td></tr>
<tr><td>secrets</td><td>1 min</td><td>Auto-generated Aurora master passwords</td></tr>
<tr><td>iam</td><td>1 min</td><td>EC2 instance profile + MSK Connect execution role</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>2. App Servers</strong></td><td>ec2 (m6i.2xlarge), ec2_pg_sink, ec2_redis_sink</td><td>3 min</td><td>3 EC2 instances (no public IP)</td></tr>
<tr><td rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle;"><strong>3. Source DB</strong></td><td>aurora_source</td><td>5&ndash;15 min</td><td>Aurora Serverless v2 source</td></tr>
<tr><td>aurora_source_limitless</td><td>20&ndash;40 min</td><td>Aurora Limitless source (shard group)</td></tr>
<tr><td rowspan="2" style="vertical-align:middle;"><strong>4. CDC Pipeline</strong></td><td>msk</td><td>30&ndash;40 min</td><td>3-broker Kafka cluster</td></tr>
<tr><td>msk_connect (Debezium source)</td><td>5&ndash;10 min</td><td>CDC streaming live</td></tr>
<tr><td rowspan="3" style="vertical-align:middle;"><strong>5. Consumers</strong></td><td>elasticache</td><td>2 min</td><td>Redis cache</td></tr>
<tr><td>aurora_sink</td><td>5&ndash;15 min</td><td>Aurora Serverless v2 sink</td></tr>
<tr><td>msk_connect_sink x5</td><td>5&ndash;10 min each</td><td>5 JDBC sink connectors writing to Aurora Sink</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>6. Final pass</strong></td><td>terraform apply</td><td>1 min</td><td>IAM tightened from <code>"*"</code> to exact ARNs</td></tr>
</table>

<p><strong>Total wall-clock time:</strong> approximately 2.5 hours for a fresh deployment.</p>

</div>

<!-- ========================================================================
     7. COST ESTIMATE
     ======================================================================== -->
<div class="WordSection2">

<h1>7. Indicative Monthly Cost</h1>

<p>Approximate cost in <code>us-west-2</code> using on-demand pricing as of May 2026. Actual costs vary with load, data transfer, and any AWS pricing changes.</p>

<table>
<tr><th>Component</th><th>Cost driver</th><th>Estimate (USD/month)</th></tr>
<tr><td>Aurora PostgreSQL Source (Serverless v2)</td><td>0.5 ACU avg &times; $0.12/ACU-hr &times; 730 hr</td><td>~$44</td></tr>
<tr><td>Aurora PostgreSQL Sink (Serverless v2)</td><td>0.5 ACU avg &times; $0.12/ACU-hr &times; 730 hr</td><td>~$44</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Aurora PostgreSQL Source Limitless</strong></td><td>16 ACU min &times; $0.12/ACU-hr &times; 730 hr</td><td><strong>~$1,400</strong></td></tr>
<tr><td>MSK Provisioned (3 brokers)</td><td>3 &times; kafka.m5.2xlarge &times; ~$0.50/hr &times; 730 hr</td><td>~$1,095</td></tr>
<tr><td>MSK Connect (6 connectors)</td><td>1&ndash;2 workers &times; 1 MCU &times; ~$0.11/MCU-hr &times; 730 hr</td><td>~$80</td></tr>
<tr><td>EC2 &mdash; app-server (m6i.2xlarge)</td><td>1 &times; ~$0.384/hr &times; 730 hr</td><td>~$280</td></tr>
<tr><td>EC2 &mdash; pg/redis sinks (x2 t3.xlarge)</td><td>2 &times; ~$0.166/hr &times; 730 hr</td><td>~$243</td></tr>
<tr><td>ElastiCache Serverless</td><td>Min 1 GB storage + 1000 ECPU/s</td><td>~$80</td></tr>
<tr><td>EBS storage (MSK brokers)</td><td>3 &times; 1000 GB &times; $0.10/GB-month</td><td>~$300</td></tr>
<tr><td>Data transfer (cross-AZ, internet egress)</td><td>Variable</td><td>$50&ndash;200</td></tr>
<tr style="background:#dbe5f1;"><td colspan="2"><strong>Estimated Total</strong></td><td><strong>~$3,673 / month</strong></td></tr>
</table>

<div class="callout">
<strong>Cost note:</strong> Aurora PostgreSQL Limitless is the largest single line item (~$1,400/month at the 16-ACU minimum, billed continuously even when idle). If the POC scope does not require Limitless, the standard <code>aurora_source</code> alone covers the CDC requirement and the monthly cost drops by approximately $1,400.
</div>

<div class="callout-info">
<strong>EC2 sizing rationale:</strong> The <code>app-server</code> runs the transaction simulator that drives the entire CDC pipeline, so it uses a heavier compute-optimized <code>m6i.2xlarge</code> (8 vCPU, 32 GiB) at ~$280/month. The <code>pg-sink-app-server</code> and <code>redis-sink-app-server</code> only consume pre-processed Kafka messages and write to the target stores, so the lighter <code>t3.xlarge</code> burstable instance suits them at ~$121/month each.
</div>

</div>

